> Is it possible to wish for a wand of wishing?

Um, in wizard mode, you CAN wish for a wand of wishing, a magic lamp,
and all sorts of other things that aren't possible in explore mode or
in a regular game.  You can wish for any dungeon feature (altars,
pits, dart traps, etc. EXCEPT staircases) in wizard mode... Let's see
a wand of wishing do THAT!  Another feature of wizard mode is that you
can always wish for any number of charges, any weapon/armor
enchantment, etc. up to 127 (spe being a signed int).  This doesn't
work with a wand of wishing in explore mode or the regular game.

In short, using explore mode to test an item is probably the best way
to go.  Use wizard mode if you need to test out something about the
dungeon or a specific situation (ie, what do I do if I'm surrounded by
a titan, black dragon, jabberwock, minotaur and a cockatrice?)

